  "diagnosis": "The errors fall into two semantic failure patterns:\n\n**1. Nuanced Qualification (False Negatives)**\nThe model misinterprets balanced or complex critiques as purely negative. It triggers on critical modifiers (e.g., \"more interesting in concept than execution\") or ambiguous emotional descriptors (e.g., \"pity\"), failing to recognize that the overall sentiment remains favorable or empathetic.\n*   **Proposed Rule:** Prioritize the primary intent/affect over qualifying clauses; recognize that \"imperfect but intriguing\" typically maps to positive sentiment.\n\n**2. Comparative Negation (False Positives)**\nThe model interprets the absence of a worst-case scenario as a positive attribute. It fails to recognize that stating something \"could have been worse\" is a backhanded compliment that confirms the subject is still poor, just not the absolute minimum.\n*   **Proposed Rule:** Identify \"lesser-of-two-evils\" constructions as negative; avoid mapping the mitigation of a negative to a positive polarity.",
